    <ImplementationPlan>
      <!--
        DESIGN (binding for implementers; authority reviews this choice)

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        EVENT KIND — command-run (foldable run/ event)
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        Shape (illustrative XML; exact attribute names free within these fields):

          run/{id}-{task}-command-run.xml
          <NgraceRunEvent graceVersion="1.0" id="N" task="T-00K" kind="command-run"
            command="bun test …"
            exitCode="0"
            assertionPassed="true"
            assertionKind="MustPassCommand"
            source="lint-run-commands" />

        Why a new kind, not a ledger section or a child of attempt:
        - Authority answer (1): foldable run/ event, append-only, digested into
          WriteEvidence on later attempts, subject to epoch membership/density.
        - Grammar already accepts any non-empty kind on Event / NgraceRunEvent
          (parseLedgerEvent only requires id, task, kind). Additive kind needs no
          NGRACE_ARTIFACT_VERSION bump (D5.2).
        - Must register kind "command-run" in KNOWN_KIND_STATE → "in-progress"
          (grace-cursor.ts) so cursor show does not degrade to
          "unrecognized event kind" when a command-run is the latest event
          (cursorStateForEventKind). That registration is a one-line allowlist
          addition, not a compatibility break.
        - Not a run-ledger-only section: companion sections skip density and are
          easier to orphan from the epoch under audit.
        - Not piggybacked on kind=attempt: attempt carries outcome/claimedConfidence
          and WriteEvidence for fix-budget semantics; mixing command evaluation into
          attempt would conflate two adjudicator surfaces and break pair checks.

        Minimum recorded fields (AC-COMMAND-EVIDENCE-RECORDED + budget honesty):
          command          — exact command text as spawned (match key; see below)
          exitCode         — numeric exit of the spawn just performed
          assertionPassed  — "true"|"false": whether the assertion evaluation
                             treated this command as a pass (for MustPassCommand
                             this equals exitCode===0; for MustPassBudget it is
                             the full budget comparison result, so exit 0 with a
                             failed metric is assertionPassed=false)
          assertionKind    — MustPassCommand | MustPassBudget
          source           — e.g. "lint-run-commands" | "assertions-final"
        Optional (do not block v1): evaluatedAt ISO, stderr digest truncated.

        Why assertionPassed beyond exitCode: AC text keys pass on exitCode 0, but
        MustPassBudget can fail the metric with exit 0. Recording only exitCode
        would label a metric-fail epoch "pass". assertionPassed is additive and
        keeps the AC's spirit (durable evaluation result) without a schema bump.
        Fold treats assertionPassed=true as the command-side pass signal;
        exitCode remains mandatory for audit.

        Writer sites:
          - evaluateMustPassCommand / evaluateMustPassBudget in assertions.ts:
            after every spawn under runCommands true (success and failure), invoke
            optional context.onCommandRun?.(payload). Discriminating negative: a
            path that returns [] on success without calling the recorder fails
            AC-COMMAND-EVIDENCE-RECORDED (today's discard).
          - lint/core.ts: when options.runCommands and options.changeId are set,
            supply onCommandRun that appends the event under the change's run/
            directory. When runCommands is false, commands are not executed and
            no evidence events are invented.
          - Layering: assertions must not import grace-cursor (cycle). Prefer
            callback injection; if a shared appendRunEvent helper is extracted to
            break the cycle, keep it additive. Stop and report only if a version
            bump is forced.

        Task attribute on the event: active cursor task for the change when known;
        otherwise T-000. Fold join does not use task for matching assertions.

        When no open epoch / covering allocation: still append when changeId +
        runCommands (operator act). Fold membership rules apply as for any loose
        event — evidence outside every Allocation is a fold error, not a silent
        ignore. Operators run --run-commands inside an open epoch.

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        MATCH KEY — exact command string equality
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        Fold joins each TargetAssertions MustPassCommand / MustPassBudget
        Command value to command-run events in the epoch being folded by
        **exact string equality** of the `command` attribute.

        Alternatives considered and rejected for v1:

        1. Normalized string (trim / collapse whitespace / reorder flags)
           Rejected: normalization can hide intentional flag or argument changes
           and invents a second "true" command string that nothing in the plan
           authored. Failures become invisible again — the class of defect this
           phase exists to eliminate.

        2. Assertion identity (file + section + index, or stable assertion id)
           Rejected for v1 as *primary* key: plan grammar has no stable assertion
           ids today; index identity silently remaps when assertions are reordered
           or inserted; matching by index while ignoring command text can accept
           old evidence for a *rewritten* command (false pass). Adding assertion
           ids is a plan-schema change outside this bundle.

        3. Recorded reference written at evaluation that names the assertion
           rather than the text (opaque token / plan path + ordinal stored on
           evidence, fold matches token only)
           Rejected as *sole* key for the same false-pass risk: after a plan edit
           replaces command A with command B at the same ordinal, token-only join
           would treat evidence for A as covering B. A recorded reference may be
           stored as an *optional* documentary attribute later; it must not be
           the adjudicator's sole match key without an authority decision.

        Chosen: exact command string equality (aligns with approved-spec
        Assumption on matching; documents the edit failure mode as an AC).

        When a command is edited between evaluation and fold:
          - Append-only evidence for the old command string remains on disk.
          - Fold looks up the *current* TargetAssertions command text.
          - Old evidence does not match → that required command has **absent
            recorded evidence** → CalibrationAdjudication outcome="pending"
            with a reason that names the ledger gap (not a live re-spawn).
          - Operator re-runs with --run-commands to record evidence for the new
            text, then folds. No silent orphaning, no false pass.
        This behaviour is pinned by AC criteria on T-002 (not an accident).

        Multiple command-run events for the same command: last-writer-wins by
        event id within the epoch (highest id). Re-runs after a fix are honest.

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        D6.5 — forbidden report-time path stays UNREACHABLE
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        - collectCalibrationReport continues to read only stored
          CalibrationAdjudication (existing corr-156 contract).
        - Fold uses a **new helper** (name illustrative:
          completeFromStructuralAndCommandEvidence / joinCommandRunEvidence)
          called only from buildCalibrationAdjudicationAtFold.
        - evaluateTargetComplete remains the structural three-valued core with
          runCommands: false hardcoded. Fold may still call it for *non-command*
          structural target issues, then join command-run records for
          MustPassCommand / MustPassBudget — or the new helper composes both.
          Either way: fold must **not** set runCommands true (D6.3(b) not
          authorized; D8.5 forbids cost-based slide to (b)).
        - evaluateTargetComplete is **not** extended with a report-reachable
          spawn path or a "use recorded evidence" mode that doctor could call.
          Unreachable in practice is not enough: the join lives on a function
          doctor does not import; dead code still reachable from doctor fails
          AC-NO-REPORT-TIME-REEVAL.
        - Fold still writes one CalibrationAdjudication with adjudicatedAt=fold
          when claimedConfidence attempts exist (AC-D65-FOLD-STILL-STORES).

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        D6.6 — evidence before fold (settled by types)
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        CalibrationRestatement carries no outcome; report keeps pending pending
        regardless of adjudicatedAt. After fold there is no honest path to a
        boolean. Therefore:
          - Recording runs at evaluation time (lint --run-commands / assertion
            opt-in), which is before fold.
          - Fold only joins existing records; it never spawns and never invents.
          - No outcome-carrying restatement is proposed or implemented.
          - Late evidence after fold is documentary only for v1 (D8.4 / D6.6).

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        FOLD JOIN SEMANTICS (completeFrom records)
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        Given claimedConfidence attempts on the epoch:
          1. Structural target evaluation with runCommands false (or equivalent
             that never spawns). Non-command assertion errors → complete false
             → outcome fail. command-not-evaluated alone does **not** freeze
             pending if matching records exist.
          2. For each MustPassCommand / MustPassBudget Command on
             TargetAssertions: find matching command-run evidence (exact
             command string; LWW by id).
             - no match → complete undefined → pending; reason names **absent
               recorded evidence** (ledger gap), not "not opted in at this process"
               alone when the defect is missing records.
             - match with assertionPassed=false (or non-zero exitCode for
               MustPassCommand) → complete false → fail.
             - all required commands matched with assertionPassed=true, and
               structural clean → complete true → pass.
          3. Always write CalibrationAdjudication adjudicatedAt=fold when claims
             exist (D6.5).

        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        EXECUTION DISCIPLINE (this bundle's own epoch when approved)
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        - Open with cursor advance --open-epoch and **no --from/--to** (defaults
          give covering headroom; never pass task ids to those flags — F8).
        - Record each cursor attempt **at the moment** verification runs; every
          attempt digests ObservedWriteScope into WriteEvidence. A fix written
          before the fail is recorded shows as an unchanged production digest
          across the pair (F9).
        - Never stage a retrospective red (git stash → record fail → unstash) —
          forbidden by F9.1. If a red is lost, say so; an honest gap is accepted.
        - Folding requires a terminal event (cursor advance --kind terminal).
          Mandatory; present in every closed bundle; not mentioned in the
          execution skill — hence written here.
        - Red-first on every task: write the failing regression against pre-fix
          code, watch it fail, then implement.
      -->
      <T-001>
        <Title>Record command-run evidence on opt-in evaluation (D6.3(c) writer)</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <Satisfies>
          <AC-COMMAND-EVIDENCE-RECORDED />
        </Satisfies>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>
            Red-first: with runCommands true, evaluateMustPassCommand (and
            MustPassBudget) today spawns, checks exitCode, and on success returns
            an empty issue list with **no durable run/ write** (assertions.ts).
            Capture that discard in a regression that fails on pre-fix code —
            assert via absence of any kind=command-run (or agreed kind) file /
            listable record after a successful opt-in evaluation against a temp
            project, not via prose alone.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            After fix: when ngrace lint (or the designated assertion surface that
            sets runCommands) evaluates MustPassCommand / MustPassBudget with
            explicit opt-in and a selected changeId, each evaluated command leaves
            a durable foldable run/ event kind=command-run under that change's
            run/ directory, recording at least command (exact text), exitCode,
            assertionPassed, assertionKind, and source. Both success and failure
            paths write a record (non-zero exitCode still produces an event with
            assertionPassed=false). Events are append-only (D9) — never rewrite
            a prior run/* file.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            Discriminating negative (AC-COMMAND-EVIDENCE-RECORDED): a path that
            runs the command and returns only lint issues (empty list on success)
            without writing a durable run/ event **fails this criterion** — that
            is today's behaviour and must not remain the sole outcome. Assert by
            keeping a regression that would pass under discard-only evaluation.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            When runCommands is false, commands are still not executed (A5.2) and
            no command-run evidence events are invented. Assert with a case that
            would fail if the writer fabricated records from plan text alone.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            M-LINT-CORE plumbing: lintGraceProject passes changeId and a recorder
            into assertion evaluation so the write is reachable from the CLI
            --run-commands path. Layering must not introduce
            assertions→grace-cursor import cycle; use callback injection and/or a
            cycle-free append helper. If implementation requires more than an
            additive event kind / attributes (forced NGRACE_ARTIFACT_VERSION bump),
            stop and report — do not ship the bump in this task.
          </Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>bun test src/artifact/assertions.test.ts src/lint/core.test.ts</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>Fold joins recorded command-run evidence; still stores adjudication (D6.3(c) / D6.5)</Title>
        <DependsOn>
          <Task>T-001</Task>
        </DependsOn>
        <Satisfies>
          <AC-FOLD-ADJUDICATES-FROM-RECORDS />
          <AC-D65-FOLD-STILL-STORES />
        </Satisfies>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>
            Red-first: with claimedConfidence attempts and TargetAssertions that
            include MustPassCommand, fold today calls evaluateTargetComplete with
            runCommands false, stores outcome=pending, and ignores any command-run
            files even if planted. Write a regression that plants matching
            command-run evidence (exitCode 0 / assertionPassed true) plus clean
            structural targets and asserts pre-fix fold still yields pending
            (or otherwise fails to pass) — proving the join is absent.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            After fix: new fold join helper (not an extension of
            evaluateTargetComplete into a report-reachable spawn path). Given
            claimedConfidence attempts, durable command-run evidence covering
            every MustPassCommand / MustPassBudget on TargetAssertions with
            assertionPassed true (and exitCode 0 for MustPassCommand), and
            structural target assertions otherwise clean, fold writes
            CalibrationAdjudication outcome="pass" adjudicatedAt="fold".
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            Given at least one matching recorded command with assertionPassed
            false (or non-zero exitCode for MustPassCommand), fold writes
            outcome="fail" adjudicatedAt="fold".
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            Given a required TargetAssertions command with **no** matching
            recorded evidence (exact command string equality), fold writes
            outcome="pending" with a reason that names **absent recorded
            evidence** (ledger gap), not a live re-spawn. Fold must not set
            runCommands true to spawn shells (D6.3(b) not authorized). A fold
            path that only calls evaluateTargetComplete with runCommands false
            and ignores existing evidence events fails this criterion.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            Match-key edit behaviour (exact string equality — pinned, not
            accidental): plant command-run evidence for command string A; change
            TargetAssertions to command string B (A ≠ B) without new evidence;
            fold must write pending (absent matching evidence for B), not pass
            on orphaned evidence for A, and not fail solely because A exists.
            Re-recording evidence for B then yields pass when structural targets
            are clean. This is the operator-visible recovery after a plan command
            edit between evaluation and fold.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            AC-D65-FOLD-STILL-STORES — assert, do not only name: fold still writes
            CalibrationAdjudication when claimedConfidence attempts exist;
            collectCalibrationReport still refuses to invent labels when the
            section is absent (pending/excluded paths unchanged in spirit). A
            "fix" that removes fold-time storage and recomputes labels at report
            time fails this criterion. Register kind=command-run in
            KNOWN_KIND_STATE as in-progress so cursor position does not degrade
            solely because the latest event is command evidence.
          </Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>bun test src/grace-cursor.test.ts</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>No report-time re-eval; historical pendings stay; suite close</Title>
        <DependsOn>
          <Task>T-001</Task>
          <Task>T-002</Task>
        </DependsOn>
        <Satisfies>
          <AC-NO-REPORT-TIME-REEVAL />
          <AC-HISTORICAL-PENDING-UNCHANGED />
          <AC-SUITE-AND-LINT />
        </Satisfies>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>
            AC-NO-REPORT-TIME-REEVAL — red-first suite form, not prose: instrument
            evaluateTargetComplete so that any call throws. collectCalibrationReport
            (as consumed by ngrace doctor) must still emit the calibration section
            from stored pairs without invoking the throw. Pre-fix this is already
            true; the regression must stay green after T-001/T-002 land and must
            fail if a future change re-introduces report-time evaluateTargetComplete
            or only "avoids" it via dead code still reachable from doctor. Unreachable
            in practice is not unreachable: assert import/call graph or the throw
            probe, not a comment.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            AC-HISTORICAL-PENDING-UNCHANGED — after this change, ngrace doctor
            (or collectCalibrationReport over this repository) still reports
            C-ADOPTION-SURFACE Epoch-1, C-PLAN-QUALITY Epoch-1, and
            C-REVIEW-LANGUAGE-SCOPE Epoch-1 as pending (bucket pending,
            adjudicatedAt=fold or equivalent durable pending presentation). Tests
            must not mutate those three archives' run-ledger.xml (read-only;
            temp copies only if a fixture needs a pending shape). Discriminating
            negative: a change that flips any of those three to included/pass
            (or rewrites their stored CalibrationAdjudication outcome) **fails
            this criterion**. Helpful "cleanup" of the three permanent pendings
            is out of scope and fails the bar (D8.4 / corr 156 / D6.6). State in
            the test name or message that flipping them to pass is the failure
            mode, so a later agent does not "fix" them.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            AC-SUITE-AND-LINT — suite green for red-first regressions covering:
            (1) run-with-opt-in writes evidence events (T-001);
            (2) fold pass/fail/pending from records including command-edit → pending
                (T-002);
            (3) throw-instrumented AC-NO-REPORT-TIME-REEVAL (this task);
            (4) historical three still pending (this task).
            bun run ngrace lint --path . is 0 errors and 0 warnings (no authorized
            scope.durable-overlap expected vs plan-less C-LEDGER-READ-ABSENCE).
            bun run validate:ci green. Red-first required; a green-only
            demonstration of any AC fails this criterion. RM-GOVERNED-PATH plan.md
            phase board may note C-CALIBRATION-COMMAND-EVIDENCE progress without
            claiming P0 complete if other P0 steps remain. Conventional-commit body
            of any landing commit names new codes if any (D5.5); do not edit
            CHANGELOG.md.
          </Criterion>
          <Criterion>
            Carried non-goals asserted by absence of implementation, not by
            Satisfies alone: no outcome-carrying CalibrationRestatement; no
            migration of the three historical pendings; no fold-time runCommands
            spawn; no NGRACE_ARTIFACT_VERSION bump. If a task or PR introduces any
            of these, this close task fails.
          </Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>bun test src/artifact/assertions.test.ts src/lint/core.test.ts src/grace-cursor.test.ts src/calibration/report.test.ts</Command>
          <Command>bun run ngrace lint --path .</Command>
          <Command>bun run validate:ci</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-003>
